                    <pre class="azure-notes-text">Exploring Azure DevOps Project Features After Creation

Once the project is set up, you will see various options on the welcome screen. Here’s what each
option

1. Invite Team Members

    •   Using this option you can add others to your project.

    •   You can only invite users who are already part of your organization.




2. Boards: Manage Work Items

    •   Using this Option you can add work items.
3. Repos: Set Up Version Control

   •   Using this option we can clone or import a repository also initialize a README file for project
       summary page.




4. Pipelines: Automate CI/CD

   •   Using this option we can connect to any git provider and deploy continuously in any
       language and platform to the cloud.
5. Test Plans: Perform Testing

    •   Using this option we can perform testing solutions using the explanatory testing toolkit.




6. Artifacts: Manage Packages

    •   Using this option we can create, discover, host, install and publish NuGet, npm,
        and Maven packages.




7. Manage your services: Control Project Visibility

    •   Using this option we can disable the visibility of services.
At this stage, you have successfully created a project on Azure DevOps using the Basic Process.</pre>
